# Audio Analysis Service — every endpoint and every error, ready to run.
#
# Works with the VS Code REST Client extension and JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Requires the stack to be running (`docker compose up`, or `pnpm dev`).
#
# The sample files referenced below do not exist in the repo; create them with:
#
#   printf 'this is definitely not audio' > /tmp/fake.mp3
#   : > /tmp/empty.mp3
#   # and any real .mp3 at /tmp/song.mp3

@api = http://localhost:4490
@uploadId = replace-me-with-an-id-from-the-first-response

### Health — the compose healthcheck target
GET {{api}}/health

### Upload an MP3 — 201 the first time
POST {{api}}/api/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="song.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< /tmp/song.mp3
------boundary--

### Upload the SAME bytes under a different name — 200, duplicate: true
# This is the whole feature: `upload.filename` is the name on record,
# `submittedFilename` is what this request called it, and `originalUploadId`
# points at the original. Nothing is stored a second time.
POST {{api}}/api/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="Copy of SONG (2).MP3"
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

< /tmp/song.mp3
------boundary--

### A text file wearing an .mp3 name — 400 INVALID_AUDIO (reason: magic_bytes)
POST {{api}}/api/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="song.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< /tmp/fake.mp3
------boundary--

### An empty file — 400 EMPTY_FILE
POST {{api}}/api/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="song.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< /tmp/empty.mp3
------boundary--

### The file under the wrong field name — 400 NO_FILE, naming the field expected
POST {{api}}/api/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="audio"; filename="song.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< /tmp/song.mp3
------boundary--

### Two file parts — 400 TOO_MANY_FILES (must answer, not hang)
POST {{api}}/api/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="a.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< /tmp/song.mp3
------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="b.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< /tmp/song.mp3
------boundary--

### Wrong method on an existing path — 404 ROUTE_NOT_FOUND
GET {{api}}/api/upload

### Not multipart at all — 415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE
POST {{api}}/api/upload
Content-Type: application/json

{ "file": "nice try" }

### List uploads, newest first
GET {{api}}/api/uploads?limit=10

### One upload
GET {{api}}/api/uploads/{{uploadId}}

### The stored bytes — ETag is the content hash
GET {{api}}/api/uploads/{{uploadId}}/file

### A byte range — 206 Partial Content, which is how a player seeks
GET {{api}}/api/uploads/{{uploadId}}/file
Range: bytes=1000-1999

### The last 500 bytes — the suffix form
GET {{api}}/api/uploads/{{uploadId}}/file
Range: bytes=-500

### A range past the end — 416, with Content-Range: bytes */<size>
GET {{api}}/api/uploads/{{uploadId}}/file
Range: bytes=99999999-

### Unknown id — 404 UPLOAD_NOT_FOUND
GET {{api}}/api/uploads/0199aaaa-bbbb-7ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee

### Malformed id — 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
GET {{api}}/api/uploads/not-a-uuid

### Limit out of range — 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
GET {{api}}/api/uploads?limit=500
